#!/bin/sh
state="${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/nexium"
[ "$1" = --force ] || [ ! -f "$state/welcome-seen" ] || exit 0
if zenity --info --title="Welcome to Nexium OS" --width=540 --text="Welcome to Nexium OS — Golden Gate desktop.

Your bottom dock opens native applications. Right-click the desktop or press Super+Space for the launcher. Super+E opens Files; Super+T opens Terminal; Alt+Tab switches windows.

Messages, Calls and NEXIUM VAULT are coming soon, not functioning communication or package clients. Mac icons are pending actual pack files; standard fallbacks are in use.

This is a live system: without persistence, changes in HOME disappear after reboot. The session does not automatically install to or change your internal disks. Native terminal administration still requires care.

Use System Information in the top panel for actual system details."; then
 mkdir -p "$state"; touch "$state/welcome-seen"
fi
